    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In the wake of an extreme weather event, the head of state confronted a crisis on the Euphrates river, where reservoir overflow and a failure of protective infrastructure had triggered widespread flooding. As homes, farms, and schools were inundated, the regime's crisis-response force launched a military evacuation operation to rescue civilians. The sovereign personally surveyed the damage, reaffirming control as diplomatic coordination with the upstream state began to restore regional stability and mitigate the flood's impact.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
