    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A predictable seasonal risk that was not mitigated escalated into a flood causation event, breaching sovereign control over natural forces. The resulting disaster impact included a tragic loss of life revealing a breakdown in public safety, as several children drowned. While state assets were mobilized for citizen rescue, the collapse of civil infrastructure in governed territories underscored the governance failure. A belated concession by the upstream sovereign followed, a delayed intervention by the source of the problem.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
